# Rule: the sheet (ADR-114)

The canonical rule is `.claude/rules/sheet.md`; this file mirrors it for Cursor.

- A section is ONE arrangement (`SHEET_ARRANGEMENTS`); chrome strings are
  lettered by renderers, never authored. A new kind is a union member, a
  renderer case and a rubric row in one commit.
- The variety law is code (`lib/sheet/composition.ts`) and every real page
  walks it in `tests/lib/sheet-composition.test.ts`. The chapter cap is on the
  PRIMARY row.
- `sheet.css` is token-only, pinned at zero in three ratchets; light re-derives
  every `--sh-*` alpha in `theme.css`.
- The first value of every knob is the house; `lib/sheet/directions.json` is
  the one registry, mirrored into the ship's `armada.toml` and asserted.
- Every client-console readout is DERIVED from the arcs registry.
- House formats are CELLS, client arcs are CARDS on the overview.
- The console imports `useStackedCardsScroll` and copies the proof stack's
  skin as `--sh-*` tokens; `.sh-root` is `overflow-x: clip`.
- `data-sh-ready` is the capture's observable; run the capture and the
  mechanical gate from PowerShell (MSYS rewrites a `/route` argument).
- A reveal in the viewport's last tenth never lands; the capture waits on 0.88.
- The negative pole is shot once and never re-shot; a wave without
  `ledger.py tick --handback` never happened.
